-------------------- SPACECRAFTER INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS ---------------------

===============================================================================
        LINUX (Ubuntu and derivatives) -- building from the git repository
===============================================================================

The source is a git repository with ONE submodule (src/EntityCore).  A plain
"Download ZIP" does not contain the submodule and will not build.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What the build needs
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- git
- CMake >= 3.12          (see cmake_minimum_required in CMakeLists.txt)
- a C++ compiler with C++20 concepts support (g++ is what the project uses)
- pkg-config             (the configure step stops with a fatal error without it)
- SDL2, SDL2_mixer, SDL2_ttf, SDL2_net  -- development packages
- Vulkan loader + headers, and a Vulkan-capable card WITH CURRENT DRIVERS
- libpng16 and zlib      -- development packages
- FFmpeg development libraries: avcodec, avformat, avutil, swscale, avfilter,
  swresample.  Any recent version: the project is built and run here against
  FFmpeg 7.1 / libavcodec 61.  (The version constraint further down this file
  is a Windows/VCPKG constraint, not a Linux one.)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Install the dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$ sudo sh install_dependancies_ubuntu.sh

(The file name is spelt "dependancies"; there is also
install_dependancies_mageia.sh.  The script needs root, and it installs a
superset of the list above.  On recent Ubuntu one package it names,
libpng16-16, has been renamed and the line fails harmlessly -- libpng-dev
already pulls in the runtime.)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Get the source, WITH the submodule
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$ git clone --recurse-submodules <repository-url> spacecrafter
~$ cd spacecrafter

If you cloned without --recurse-submodules:

~$ git submodule update --init

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Build and install
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$ sh install_src.sh -j<number of cores you want to use>

The script erases build/, configures a Release build, compiles, and then runs
`sudo cmake --install` -- so it will ask for your password and it writes into
/usr/local (the binary into /usr/local/bin, the data into
/usr/local/share/spacecrafter).  To rebuild after a `git pull` without erasing
the build directory:

~$ sh install_src.sh --update -j<n>

New source files are picked up automatically (the source list is globbed with
CONFIGURE_DEPENDS); if you use your own build directory made by an older
checkout, re-run cmake once.

Use `BUILD=LocalRelease sh install_src.sh -j<n>` to compile for the CPU that is
installed right now (-march=native); the result must be recompiled if the CPU
is replaced.  localinstall_src.sh does the same thing without the variable.

THE DATA DIRECTORY IS FIXED AT COMPILE TIME.  It is /usr/local/share/spacecrafter/,
written into the binary as CONFIG_DATA_DIR in src/spacecrafter.hpp.  Passing
-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX to cmake changes where the files are COPIED and not where
the program LOOKS, so an installation outside /usr/local needs that constant
changed as well.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. The data the repository does NOT contain
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository installs the program, the compiled shaders, and eleven small
metadata files (default_config.ini, default_ssystem.ini, name.fab, zone.tab and
the like).  It contains NO textures, NO star catalogues, NO sky cultures, NO
landscapes, NO fonts, NO audio, NO scripts, NO 3D models, NO translations and
NO videos.  Those are delivered separately and have to be present under
/usr/local/share/spacecrafter/ (textures/ and stars/ at the top level, the rest
under data/) before the program is useful.

If they are missing, the program still starts and its log still says
"Completed copy of textures", "Completed copy of scripts" and so on -- the
message is printed whether the copy worked or not.  Check that
~/.spacecrafter/textures/ and the other directories are not empty.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. First run
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$ spacecrafter

The first run creates ~/.spacecrafter itself and fills it in -- 19 directories
and 7 files, config.ini among them -- and the log of that run is
~/.spacecrafter/log/spacecrafter.log.

Configuration is ~/.spacecrafter/config.ini.  Note that upgrading to a build
with a different version string makes the program rewrite that file by itself:
comments are dropped and any key it does not know is deleted.  Keep a copy
aside before upgrading if you have edited it by hand.

===============================================================================
        COMPILATION from the source package (spacecrafterXXXX-master.zip)
===============================================================================
If you can't find a suited binary package or if you are curious you can also
compile the software by yourself.

Make sure you install all the necessary dependencies.

Launch install_dependancies_ubuntu.sh or install_dependancies_mageia.sh

Spacecrafter requires :

- Cmake > v3.3
- SDL2-dev
- SDL2_mixer-dev
- SDL2_net-dev
- SDL2_ttf-dev
- Vulkan libraries
- FFMPEG (VCPKG => 5.1.2#10) (required => avcodec-59.dll, avformat-59.dll, avutil-57.dll, swscale-6.dll, swresample-4.dll) (higher versions crash)
- libvpx (VCPKG => 1.15.2) (required => libvpx build with ffmpeg (no dll for that lib everything will be in ffmpeg dlls))

FFMPEG and libvpx can be installed using VCPKG:
.\vcpkg install ffmpeg[avcodec,avdevice,avfilter,avformat,swresample,swscale,vpx]:x64-windows libvpx:x64-windows --overlay-ports=$overlay --recurse
(-overlay-ports is the path to the folder where you unzipped the portfiles to use to compile ffmpeg 5.1.2#10, if you don't use it you will get the last version of ffmpeg that crash with spacecrafter)
(-recurse is used to rebuild ffmpeg with libvpx support in case you alredy had ffmpeg installed)

Once they are installed you are ready to compile Spacecrafter sources:

Unzip the archive:
~$ unzip spacecrafterXXXX-master.zip
~$ cd spacecrafterXXXX-master
~$ sh install_dependancies_<type your OS ubuntu or mageia>.sh

Then type:
~$ sh install_src.sh -j<number of core you have on your computer>

Then to launch the software type:
~$ spacecrafter
